# doom_touch_cases.pdl - proofs for the doom touch handler in pc_menu_input.c (events go through play_event.sh when the page's verb equals the tile's cmds=; otherwise the old direct verb path). Run with auto's case_run and env  NEW=<driver built from the new pc_menu_input.c>  OLD=<driver built from the previous version>  R=<scratch house>  AP=$R/@.apps/piececraft-hq  D=$AP/pieces/system/maps/doom  SRC=<real piececraft-hq dir, read only>  SETUP=<the setup command used in each case>  ST=<the state-print command>. Real data: desk e1m8_anomaly. Tiles: (93,15) page verb == cmds (change_ammo); (101,73) page says change_armor but cmds=change_hp; (33,42) has no event folder.
# CASE | name | expected exit code | must contain ONE substring (- none) | must NOT contain ONE substring (- none) | command (sh -c)
CASE | t1 agreeing tile: effect happens once (ammo 50 to 60) | 0 | ammo=60 | ammo=70 | eval "$SETUP"; ( cd "$NEW" && ./drv "$AP" 93 15 ); eval "$ST"
CASE | t2 disagreeing tile keeps the old behaviour (hp +10, armor 0) | 0 | hp=110 | armor=1 | eval "$SETUP"; ( cd "$NEW" && ./drv "$AP" 101 73 ); eval "$ST"
CASE | t3 tile without an event folder keeps the old behaviour (ammo 60) | 0 | ammo=60 | ammo=70 | eval "$SETUP"; ( cd "$NEW" && ./drv "$AP" 33 42 ); eval "$ST"
CASE | t4 debugger paused: agreeing tile is queued and nothing ran | 0 | queued: 1 | ammo=60 | eval "$SETUP"; printf "paused=1\n" > "$R/#.desktop/blueprintz_debug.txt"; ( cd "$NEW" && ./drv "$AP" 93 15 ); eval "$ST"
CASE | t5 play off: nothing happens | 0 | state:  queued: 0 | ammo=60 | eval "$SETUP"; printf "mode=off\n" > "$R/#.desktop/khtpm_play_mode.state.txt"; ( cd "$NEW" && ./drv "$AP" 93 15 ); eval "$ST"
CASE | c4 control: the OLD handler ignores the pause (ammo 60, nothing queued) | 0 | ammo=60 | queued: 1 | eval "$SETUP"; printf "paused=1\n" > "$R/#.desktop/blueprintz_debug.txt"; ( cd "$OLD" && ./drv "$AP" 93 15 ); eval "$ST"
